# Web Frontend Conventions

## Tech Stack

- **Framework:** React 19 + Vite 6 (SPA)
- **Routing:** react-router-dom v7 (createBrowserRouter)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 with semantic design tokens
- **Icons:** lucide-react
- **Linting:** Biome (single quotes, no semicolons, 2-space indent)
- **Testing:** Vitest + Testing Library

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` (from root) — starts both server and Vite dev server
- `pnpm --filter @ts-media-server/web dev` — Vite dev server only
- `pnpm --filter @ts-media-server/web build` — production build
- `pnpm --filter @ts-media-server/web typecheck` — tsc --noEmit

## Key Patterns

- Path alias: `~/` maps to `web/src/`
- API calls go through `~/lib/api.ts` — never use raw `fetch` in components
- Use `useFetch` hook for data loading (auto-cancels stale requests)
- Custom primitives in `~/components/primitives/` — no UI library
- Semantic color tokens via CSS custom properties (see `index.css`)
- Dark-first: default theme is dark, light mode via class toggle

## File Organization

- `src/pages/` — route-level components (one per route)
- `src/components/` — shared components
- `src/components/primitives/` — low-level UI building blocks
- `src/hooks/` — custom React hooks
- `src/lib/` — utilities, API client

## Style Rules

- Use semantic token classes (`text-foreground`, `bg-surface`) not raw palette (`text-slate-900`)
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes over custom CSS
- Component files: `kebab-case.tsx`
